    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but when you talk about \"challenging harmful narratives\" and \"fixing broken structures,\" it feels like you're describing a specific kind of political activism rather than just general virtues. isn't there a risk that these \"virtues\" just become a way to label anyone who disagrees with a certain social or political agenda as being \"immoral\" or \"unvirtuous\"?",
